@startuml
title Meridian End-to-End Weather Reading Trace

actor "Field Station" as Field
participant "Ingest\n(C)" as Ingest
database "SQLite Store" as DB
participant "Analytics Orchestrator\n(Python)" as Orch
participant "Crop Model\n(Fortran)" as Crop
participant "Output Parser\n(Python)" as Parser
participant "REST API\n(Java)" as API
participant "Operator Console\n(JavaScript / jQuery)" as Console
participant "Views\n(trends, compare, forecast,\nanomalies, quality)" as Views
participant "Meridian.Forecast\n(util/forecast.js)" as Forecast
participant "Meridian.Quality\n(util/quality.js)" as Quality

Field -> Ingest : 44-byte binary telemetry frame
note right of Ingest
  Big-endian format
  MRD1 header
  Station ID
  Year + day-of-year
  TMAX, TMIN, RAIN,
  SRAD, RH, WIND
end note

Ingest -> DB : INSERT OR REPLACE reading
note right of DB
  SQLite reading row
  stnid, year, doy,
  tmax, tmin, rain,
  srad, rh, wind, flags
end note

DB --> Orch : SELECT weather readings
note right of Orch
  SQL rows converted to
  Python Reading objects
end note

Orch -> Crop : MERIDIAN.DAT
note right of Crop
  Fixed-width text deck
  DOY, TMAX, TMIN,
  RAIN, SRAD
end note

Crop --> Parser : MERIDIAN.OUT
note right of Parser
  Fixed-width text output
  DOY, SW, ET,
  DRAIN, BIOM, LAI
end note

Parser -> DB : INSERT forecast data
note right of DB
  SQLite forecast and
  forecast_daily rows
end note

Console -> API : GET /api/series?station=ID&year=YYYY
note right of API
  HTTP GET request
  Query parameters:
  station, year
end note

API -> DB : SELECT forecast_daily rows
DB --> API : SQLite query result
API --> Console : HTTP 200 application/json
note right of Console
  JSON array of forecast objects
end note

Console -> Console : Parse JSON into JavaScript objects
Console -> Views : rows

' --- CHANGED: views now call shared utilities ---
Views -> Forecast : currentRun(rows)\n[forecast.js, trends.js, anomalies.js]
Forecast --> Views : current forecast run / default year
Views -> Forecast : spread(rows, preserveOrder)\n[trends.js, compare.js]
Forecast --> Views : min, max, current yield,\ncurrent year, run count, history
Views -> Quality : RULES, FLAG_LABELS\n[quality.js view; FLAG_LABELS also anomalies.js]
Quality --> Views : QC thresholds and flag labels

Views -> Views : Format numeric value
Views -> Views : Render HTML DOM / bar chart
@enduml